    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36769" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξανα-χωρέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go out of the way, withdraw, retreat,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὸν ποταμόν, πρὸς τὸ ὄρος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.207
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				5.101
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.229
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ τῶν φορτίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.196
				</span></i>
			; of a plant, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[γῆς] συνημερουμένης
			ἐ.</span> Thprh.<i><span class="en">
				<u>HP</u>
				6.3.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξανεχώρει τὰ εἰρημένα</span>
			<i>sought to back out of</i> his words, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.28
			</span></i>.</div>
